delimiter $ ( ) $;
provable sort wff;
term K: wff;
term G: wff;
term link (a: wff): wff;
prefix link: $L$ prec 40;
term need (a: wff): wff;
prefix need: $N$ prec 40;
axiom lk: $ L K $;
axiom nk: $ N K $;
-- Two-hyp rule whose binder `a` appears only in the hypotheses (the conclusion
-- `G` pins nothing). Hyp `L a` is fillable from the ref pool (pins `a`); hyp
-- `N a` has no matching ref, so it must be generated — and generation only
-- works once `a` is pinned by the sibling. This is the binder-pinning case the
-- generator slot ordering must get right.
axiom r (a: wff): $ L a $ > $ N a $ > $ G $;
theorem t: $ G $;
